abstract: "Integer-day calendars for replenishment with fixed turnover times. Rounding the event times of logarithmically phased power-of-two clocks gives a feasible calendar costing at most 1/ln 2 (about 1.4427) times the optimum for any monotone submodular daily cost, improving the factor two of Bosman et al. (2022) on trees; 1/ln 2 is exact for calendars repeating within the longest turnover time. Constant-gap calendars with dividing gaps have best worst-case factor between 1.6001 and 1.6014. Exact structural bounds and certificates included. Unrefereed candidate; internal AI-assisted review only; priority not claimed (an unobtained 2025 thesis). Text and data CC0-1.0; code MIT."
